#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:5
#: 5312d76888da421d819d7fbbdbd0176b
msgid "Loweheiser Generator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:9
#: 70c64e8d764647a3ac8a42bebf005b6e
msgid "The `Loweheiser Hybgen <https://www.loweheiser.com/hybrid-drone-generators/>`__ is an electric generator that can be installed into a multirotor drone to extend the flight time. This hybrid powertrain is suitable for drones up to 25 kg MTOM that require long flight times or heavy payloads. It consists of a two-stroke combustion engine of 32cc with a permanent-magnet generator attached to the crankshaft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:12
#: c5d881a65e7c4b71b9066d810acbf76e
msgid "Compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:14
#: 87959f7ee772460d8790a356ec12240f
msgid "the driver for this device is not included by default in the firmware built and available on the `Firmware Server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ . Either the user must build his own firmware with this backend enabled or use the `Custom Firmware Server <https://custom.ardupilot.org>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:19
#: 340850bd162c4ff68448c6f47b1debde
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:22
#: 4d1a39bc84aa4f0da937ea68a6d6cbec
msgid "Parameter configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:24
#: 01f0e39b0ca742a09e5b9beb28d851b0
msgid "This generator is a serial device. Connect it to a serial port of the flight controller and set the corresponding ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL=2`` (MAVLink). Also set  the corresponding ``MAVx_OPTIONS`` bit 1 (Don’t forward mavlink to/from)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:26
#: 8f7b904fd596492d9619cc299371d3bb
msgid "Set :ref:`EFI_TYPE <EFI_TYPE>` = 4 (Loweheiser) and :ref:`GEN_TYPE <GEN_TYPE>` = 4 (Loweheiser). Restart the flight controller to load the rest of the generator and EFI parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:29
#: 76ecc65650bd4aa79368d890f7eaa404
msgid "Configure a 3-position switch on an RC input channel with ``RCx_OPTION=85`` (Generator). This will act as the generator state control switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:31
#: 1c0db37f8d544fb6bfcb0a7f29530b67
msgid "(OPTIONAL) Configure an analog RC input channel (not a switch) with ``RCy_OPTION=218`` (Loweheiser throttle). This will act as manual throttle input for the generator throttle body. It is encouraged to use your throttle stick to drive this input channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:33
#: 98b7d8d009ee4d6ab0f112d18c52062b
msgid "(OPTIONAL) Configure an switch-type RC input channel with ``RCz_OPTION=111`` (Loweheiser starter). This is a switch that will control the generator starter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:35
#: 757b45cdd8fb477eb05eb132bd90a6fb
msgid "There is no need to configure output channels, as the generator is operated entirely through the serial port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:37
#: 2903ffea804a4a24bac284f5b4126215
msgid "To monitor the generator performance, configure a battery monitor with ``BATTx_TYPE=17`` (Generator-Elec). To monitor the engine performance, configure a battery monitor with ``BATTy_TYPE=18`` (Generator-Fuel). Set the volume of the fuel in the tank in ``BATTy_CAPACITY`` (in mL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:39
#: 6140ee67fc784136a01ca58fb127e839
msgid ":ref:`GEN_L_IDLE_TH <GEN_L_IDLE_TH>` can be used to adjust the throttle percent that will be sent to the generator throttle body during idling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:41
#: f1794fd3d9874bb0b1b9f5b11dffecb1
msgid ":ref:`GEN_L_IDLE_TH_H <GEN_L_IDLE_TH_H>` can be used to adjust the throttle percent that will be sent to the generator throttle body, during warming up or cooldown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:43
#: 5c7052ad7b2149709321e837730da0a5
msgid "The following parameters can be used to adjust the temperature limits of the generator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:45
#: f5d06d8cdfcd47ecb0d828c16627b0f9
msgid ":ref:`GEN_L_RUN_TEMP <GEN_L_RUN_TEMP>`: The cylinder head temperature required for the generator to start producing power, in deg Celsius."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:46
#: 03b423c2160d4c5e990cc52d7a57f651
msgid ":ref:`GEN_L_IDLE_TEMP <GEN_L_IDLE_TEMP>`: The cylinder head temperature required for the generator to return to idle after having run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:47
#: 3526d7c07f9542e8a7c513ffcccd8857
msgid ":ref:`GEN_L_OVER_TEMP <GEN_L_OVER_TEMP>`: The cylinder head overheat temperature. Above this threshold a warning message gets sent over MAVLink"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:49
#: 58267371940e45be8d7441118d3cb3ee
msgid "The following parameters are not yet supported by the generator manufacturer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:51
#: 115dd159f15e43eabf36f3859b225498
msgid ":ref:`GEN_L_MNT_TIME <GEN_L_MNT_TIME>`: Seconds until maintenance is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:52
#: 6909448eeda14180bc54cc75db40a5ce
msgid ":ref:`GEN_L_RUNTIME <GEN_L_RUNTIME>`: Total time this generator has run, in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:55
#: d0637d3bc5d9418eba94ae1840d74149
msgid "Controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:57
#: 2e7b94537b3b4be99277630ea276920b
msgid "The switch configured as Generator has 3 values: STOP, IDLE, RUNNING. Begin on the STOP command. The generator is stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:59
#: 6e60ffe244f448acb0cc693b433da4ec
msgid "Set the generator switch to IDLE. The goal of the IDLE state is to start the engine and bring it up to temperature. If you have configured a Loweheiser throttle input channel, you can now use it to select the throttle during IDLE state. Otherwise, ``GEN_IDLE_TH`` will be applied. If you have configured a Loweheiser starter input channel, you can now use it to activate the starter motor and crank the engine. Otherwise, crank the engine manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:63
#: ff664d302b6c4725b0e6892be3e714f8
msgid "Set the generator switch to RUNNING. The driver will actually wait until the engine reaches a temperature of ``GEN_RUN_TEMP``, before it switches to the RUN state. Until then, it will set the throttle to ``GEN_IDLE_TH_H``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:65
#: df322fd9b1ee4959a8e6cfcc4165039a
msgid "Once temperature is reached, the generator will proceed to the RUN state. In this state the throttle is controlled automatically by a governor and the generator produces power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:67
#: 32ba2d248349452cae9f70e13c60c698
msgid "To stop the engine, set the Generator switch to STOP. The driver will actually wait until the engine cools down to a temperature of ``GEN_IDLE_TEMP`` before it stops. During that time, it will apply ``GEN_IDLE_TH_H`` throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:69
#: 9d0a4045cf9f4a7283d663684a72fa79
msgid "No state transitions will take place once the vehicle is armed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loweheiser-generator.rst:71
#: 1a8ea6c5a6eb4828b3546dec599cc298
msgid "The Loweheiser driver will apply additional pre-arm checks, to ensure safety of operations."
msgstr ""

